WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.579
Welcome to Module 6 In this module

00:00:03.789 --> 00:00:05.211
we are going to move from writing

00:00:05.224 --> 00:00:07.776
small pieces of Python code toward organizing

00:00:07.803 --> 00:00:09.697
larger programs in a cleaner and more

00:00:09.711 --> 00:00:12.618
reusable way Up to this point you

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:15.724
have worked with variables conditions loops
functions

00:00:15.895 --> 00:00:20.079
lists tuples dictionaries and sets Those tools

00:00:20.105 --> 00:00:21.947
are very useful but as a program

00:00:21.961 --> 00:00:23.842
becomes larger we also need a way

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:27.013
to organize the code itself If everything

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:29.118
is placed inside one long script the

00:00:29.145 --> 00:00:31.737
program can become difficult to read difficult

00:00:31.763 --> 00:00:34.829
to test and difficult to update This

00:00:34.855 --> 00:00:38.895
module introduces four important ideas The first

00:00:38.921 --> 00:00:41.855
is a module A module is usually

00:00:41.882 --> 00:00:44.645
one Python file that contains reusable code

00:00:45.566 --> 00:00:48.513
The second is a package A package

00:00:48.539 --> 00:00:52.132
groups related modules together The third is

00:00:52.158 --> 00:00:54.947
a class A class is a blueprint

00:00:54.974 --> 00:00:58.421
that combines related data and behavior The

00:00:58.434 --> 00:01:01.382
fourth is an object An object is

00:01:01.408 --> 00:01:03.895
one actual instance created from a class

00:01:04.829 --> 00:01:06.197
The goal is not to become an

00:01:06.211 --> 00:01:09.724
advanced software engineer in this module The

00:01:09.737 --> 00:01:12.487
goal is much simpler I want you

00:01:12.513 --> 00:01:14.724
to understand how Python projects can be

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.539
organized as they grow You will see

00:01:17.566 --> 00:01:21.079
several executable Python examples throughout the
slides

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.724
When you reach a code slide you

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.395
can click the Run button below the

00:01:25.421 --> 00:01:28.329
editor The first time you run Python

00:01:28.342 --> 00:01:29.737
in the browser it may take a

00:01:29.763 --> 00:01:31.908
few seconds for the Python environment to

00:01:31.921 --> 00:01:34.947
load After that the code should run

00:01:34.974 --> 00:01:37.592
more quickly As you move through the

00:01:37.618 --> 00:01:40.026
module focus on the big idea behind

00:01:40.053 --> 00:01:42.789
each example We want code that is

00:01:42.816 --> 00:01:45.566
easier to reuse easier to understand and

00:01:45.579 --> 00:01:46.737
easier to maintain
